A key semantic risk is emerging in the AI throttle: its state advances on redirected method invocations, not on goal ticks. That distinction matters because one target method has five invocation sites; I’m checking the pinned IoB bytecode’s control flow and the compiled release classes to determine whether cadence can vary by branch or multiple calls per tick.
