      "id": "F-001",
      "severity": "P1_HIGH",
      "category": "CPU/MSPT and behavior",
      "title": "The AI interval is counted per redirected invocation, not per goal tick",
      "locations": [
        "src/main/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/mixin/DragonFlyAndAttackAirbourneTargetGoalMixin.java:40",
        "src/main/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/mixin/DragonFollowPlayerFlyingMixin.java:39",
        "src/main/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/mixin/UntamedDragonCircleFlightGoalMixin.java:54",
        "src/main/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/config/PerformanceConfig.java:83"
      ],
      "causal_explanation": "Each counter advances only when execution reaches a redirected moveTo/circleEntity call. DragonFollowPlayerFlying has five static invocation sites sharing one counter, while goal ticks containing no eligible invocation do not advance it. Consequently ai_move_interval_ticks measures eligible call occurrences, and can advance more than once in a tick if more than one site executes. This is not a stable N-tick cadence despite the config name and tick-based documentation.",
      "impact": "Movement correction frequency becomes branch-dependent. The first request is immediate, but subsequent requests are not demonstrably separated by the configured number of server ticks.",
      "exact_repair": "Track cadence once at tick() HEAD and cache one allow/deny decision for the whole tick. Preserve first-eligible-request behavior with an armed/cooldown state, allow all intended calls on a due tick, reset the state at WrappedGoal start/stop, and keep the counter bounded to avoid integer overflow. Alternatively rename the option and documentation to an eligible-request-count interval if that behavior is intentional."
    },
    {
      "id": "F-002",
      "severity": "P1_HIGH",
      "category": "Tests and Mixin correctness",
      "title": "Tests do not prove transformed interval, return-value, lifecycle, or constant-site semantics",
      "locations": [
        "src/test/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/verification/AiMoveCadenceFixture.java:12",
        "src/test/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/verification/GameplayBytecodeFixture.java:32",
        "src/test/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/verification/MixinLifecycleFixture.java:23",
        "src/test/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/verification/RendererBytecodeFixture.java:61"
      ],
      "causal_explanation": "AiMoveCadenceFixture tests only the pure modulo predicate. GameplayBytecodeFixture counts static invocation and bipush instructions but does not analyze branch exclusivity, calls per tick, whether moveTo's boolean result controls downstream behavior, or whether constants are the intended modulo divisors. MixinLifecycleFixture reflects untransformed mixin classes rather than exercising a transformed WrappedGoal. The required original IoB JAR is absent from this frozen checkout, so those upstream fixtures are not independently reproducible here.",
      "impact": "A redirect can return false on a skipped call and alter caller control flow, or cadence can vary by branch, while all present fixtures still pass.",
      "exact_repair": "Add an ASM-based target test that verifies control flow and return-value consumption, plus post-Mixin transformed-bytecode checks. Add an integration fixture covering zero, one, and multiple eligible calls per tick; start/stop/restart; disabled and interval-1 modes; config reload; and long-lived counter behavior. Verify the egg and shock constants by their IREM/packet/damage dataflow, not only literal counts. Pin and record the tested IoB dependency digest."
    },
    {
      "id": "F-003",
      "severity": "P2_MEDIUM",
      "category": "Hot-path overhead",
      "title": "Default throttled requests perform repeated Forge config lookups",
      "locations": [
        "src/main/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/config/PerformanceConfig.java:76",
        "src/main/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/config/PerformanceConfig.java:86",
        "src/main/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/mixin/ADragonEggBaseMixin.java:18",
        "src/main/java/network/vonix/isleofberkperformance/mixin/ShockEffectMixin.java:22"
      ],
      "causal_explanation": "At the default settings, shouldRunAiMove(int) reads the enabled value once and the interval value twice for every redirected request. Egg and shock injectors also read ForgeConfigSpec values from recurring gameplay paths. The release bytecode confirms the duplicate get()/unboxing path.",
      "impact": "The patch adds config-access overhead to the same hot paths it is intended to reduce. No claim is made that this outweighs avoided navigation work, but it is unnecessary.",
      "exact_repair": "Snapshot each setting once per goal tick or maintain validated volatile primitive caches updated by Forge config load/reload events. Test reload visibility and avoid caching values only at class initialization."
    },
